1️⃣ useEffect to load notes from localStorage
useEffect(() => {
  const storedNotes = localStorage.getItem("notes");
  if (storedNotes) {
    setNotes(JSON.parse(storedNotes));
  }
}, []);

Explanation:

useEffect(() => { ... }, [])
useEffect is a React hook that runs after the component renders.
The empty array [] means it only runs once, when the page/component loads.
localStorage.getItem("notes")
This tries to read the string stored in the browser’s localStorage under the key "notes".
localStorage is like a small permanent storage in the browser — data stays even after page reload.
if (storedNotes)
Checks if there actually is any saved data.
setNotes(JSON.parse(storedNotes))
storedNotes is stored as a string in localStorage.
JSON.parse converts it back into a JavaScript array of objects.
setNotes(...) updates the React state so your notes display on the page immediately.

✅ Effect: When you open/reload the page, any previously saved notes are automatically loaded and displayed.

2️⃣ Creating a new note
const handleCreateNote = () => {
  const newNote = { id: Date.now(), title: "New Note", content: "" };

  setNotes(prevNotes => {
    const updatedNotes = [...prevNotes, newNote];
    localStorage.setItem("notes", JSON.stringify(updatedNotes)); // sync with localStorage
    return updatedNotes;
  });
};

Explanation:
 
const newNote = { id: Date.now(), title: "New Note", content: "" };
Creates a new note object with:
id: unique number using Date.now()
title: "New Note"
content: empty for now
setNotes(prevNotes => { ... })
Functional state update — React provides prevNotes, the current state of notes.
This is safer than using setNotes([...notes, newNote]) because React state updates asynchronously.
Ensures you don’t accidentally overwrite the latest notes if multiple updates happen quickly.
const updatedNotes = [...prevNotes, newNote];
Adds the new note to the existing notes array.
localStorage.setItem("notes", JSON.stringify(updatedNotes));
Converts the updatedNotes array into a string (JSON) and saves it in localStorage.
This makes your notes persistent across page reloads.
return updatedNotes;
Updates the React state with the new array of notes.
The UI automatically re-renders with the new note.


अब 2 type state चाहिन्छ:

1. notes → saved notes (list मा देखिने)
2. draft → अहिले लेखिरहेको note (temporary)

